Freestanding stand-ins for the C++ standard headers that atomic_queue.h
and defs.h include: only what they use. <atomic> is built on clang's
__atomic builtins, as libstdc++'s is. The allocator-based queues
(AtomicQueueB, AtomicQueueB2) are declared but never instantiated, so
<memory> declares only what their definitions name.
